# Store and check out text as LF on every platform. Without eol=lf a Windows
# checkout produces CRLF while CI produces LF, and since a .unitypackage embeds
# file bytes verbatim the same commit would build to different packages. Pinning
# LF keeps the build reproducible everywhere and makes the result independent of
# each contributor's core.autocrlf setting.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.cs      text diff=csharp
*.asmdef  text
*.meta    text
*.json    text
*.md      text
*.yml     text
*.py      text

# Managed plugins must never be line-ending converted.
*.dll binary

# Sprite sheets and pet sounds. text=auto already detects these as binary, so
# this is a guard against the blanket rule above rather than a fix.
*.png binary
*.wav binary

# Built packages are gitignored. This is a guard for the blanket rule above: if
# one is ever force-added, it must not be line-ending converted.
*.unitypackage binary
